From e8e06dfb0e512e0b75ccb95ef9551cd74b479857 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:17:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give the complete guardian suite a moderate deadline

The Intel Mac guardian suite exceeded its 60-second whole-binary limit in
native job 117096549690. A diagnostic run with a 300-second deadline
completes all 123 tests in 54.1 seconds and Bazel identifies that duration
as outside its SHORT range. Use the moderate deadline for this suite.

Bazel's timeout attribute is nonconfigurable. Retain one shared suite and
keep faster-platform sizing advisories visible. Compiler warning policy,
all test bodies, and every assertion remain unchanged.

Base: rust-v0.163.0 (83086188ae0614bd882818ff1aa23f3194962012), with the
maintained queue through 0057. Native red: 60-second cancellation before
completion. Native diagnostic green: run 38955622801, guardian invocation
0e8ff237-4a12-410a-9202-7512c5b708e4, 123 passed, zero failed or ignored.
Authoring verification: maintained just fmt-check passes. Maintained
run-bazel-ci.sh test executes all 123 tests on Linux in 9.52 seconds,
6579 cached actions and two sandbox actions. The fast-platform moderate
sizing advisory remains visible. Fresh emitted-patch and full native CI
acceptance remain required in the active CI repair execution record.
---
 codex-rs/ext/guardian-v2/BUILD.bazel | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/codex-rs/ext/guardian-v2/BUILD.bazel b/codex-rs/ext/guardian-v2/BUILD.bazel
index e10e27c05..f5b14edd4 100644
--- a/codex-rs/ext/guardian-v2/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/codex-rs/ext/guardian-v2/BUILD.bazel
@@ -11,4 +11,5 @@ codex_rust_crate(
     crate_name = "codex_guardian_v2",
     extra_binaries = ["//codex-rs/code-mode-host:codex-code-mode-host"],
     test_data_extra = glob(["src/**/snapshots/**"]),
+    unit_test_timeout = "moderate",
 )
-- 
